@nsobid-F19B2E01E1794F933A9720C1404BB6F6

# Bayonetta 2 1.2 - Disable DLAA

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the post-process anti-aliasing pass. Bayonetta 2 has no FXAA or
// SMAA; its post AA is DLAA, run as the FilterShaderDLAA1 (edge detection) and
// FilterShaderDLAA2 (blend) passes after the final composite.
//
// One graphics flag bit decides whether they run. When it is clear, the frame
// function draws the composite straight to the output and returns; when it is
// set, it draws the same composite and then the two DLAA passes on top.
// Removing the bit test makes every frame take the first path, so the output
// is the engine's own no-AA image rather than a new code path.
//
// This patches the frame code, not the flag, so scene settings that set the
// bit cannot turn it back on.

@enabled
00979EFC 1F2003D5   // NOP (was TBNZ W8,#1 = the DLAA enable bit)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Bayonetta 2 1.2 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_010, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
